I left out both of the operations team's requests: the log line and the metadata fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a filesystem capability, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need an `HTTPClient` handle allowing that host. The node holds neither, and the target has no WASI adapter. The fetch would also send untrusted feed text to an internal service. If operations needs these, the graph has to grant them, for example a `Notifier`/`EventEmitter` sink for the log and an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` for the fetch. That change belongs in the graph, not this node's body.

